    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate looking to leverage several high-floor matchups against middle-of-the-road pitching, with **Taylor Ward** headlining our lineup. **Taylor Ward** earns the day's highest efficiency score (67.54) primarily due to a premium park factor (+16%) and a favorable leadoff spot, making him an elite play against Canning. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a high-octane engine despite a moderate matchup against a tough arm in Flaherty; his raw talent and +8% order bonus anchor the UTIL spot with a 66.03 score. Meanwhile, the Cubs\u2019 staff provides a target-rich environment for our hitters, as **Luis Arraez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman** all benefit from the +15% SP skill adjustment against Assad. Notably, **Gavin Sheets** provides surprising value today (63.36) as his combination of a hitter-friendly park and a +7% platoon edge creates a significant ceiling despite his middle-of-the-order positioning.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Bryson Stott**. While **Bryson Stott** posted a respectable 48.37 score, he was ultimately squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-scoring options facing softer pitching. His matchup against Misiorowski is marred by a challenging 2.79 xERA, which significantly depressed his skill adjustment (-19%) compared to **Geraldo Perdomo**, whose efficiency sits at 62.54 due to a favorable look at Lodolo. **Masyn Winn** also fell short of the start threshold, yielding to our higher-upside outfield and middle infield depth. As we track the day, monitor **Jonathan Aranda**; while he sports a 59.80 score, the dynamic platoon penalty (-12%) against Aldegheri is a volatility risk. With **Cal Raleigh** sidelined on the IL, we are managing our bench tightly to preserve our remaining game caps for higher-leverage windows later in the week.",
